    "text": {
      "L1": "A number with more digits is bigger, so every 4-digit number is bigger than every 3-digit number.",
      "L2": "To compare numbers with the same number of digits, start from the left.",
      "L3": "Compare thousands first, then hundreds, tens, and ones.",
      "L4": "As soon as one place is different, that place decides; later digits do not matter.",
      "L5": "For 6482 and 6428, thousands and hundreds match, so compare the tens.",
      "L6": "Eight tens is more than two tens, so 6482 is bigger than 6428.",
      "L7": "On a number line, spacing shows value. 1000 is one tenth of the way from 0 to 10000.",
